notes:
I found two free options, both run in Halton Hills by the operators themselves.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Kids & Me drop-in neighbourhood group, Halton Hills Public Library, Acton Branch",
      "age_fit": "families with babies or children up to 6 years of age",
      "when": "Thursdays 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.; follows the school calendar, starting the second week of September, closed statutory holidays and school breaks",
      "price": "Free",
      "source_name": "Halton Region"
    },
    {
      "name": "EarlyON Child and Family Centres, Links2Care (Acton and Georgetown)",
      "age_fit": "children from birth to their 6th birthday with a parent or caregiver",
      "source_name": "Links2Care"
    }
  ]
}
```

- **Kids & Me:** Halton Region's page lists the Acton Branch session. It lists other Kids & Me sessions too, but those are in other towns, so I left them out. The page describes it as a free weekly drop-in. It does not say whether the Acton group is currently running.
- **EarlyON:** Links2Care's page describes free drop-in, registered and online programs. Its current schedule is on that page and I did not read it, so no day, time or registration detail is given.
- **Left out:** The Halton Hills Gymnastics Centre preschool drop-in (under 4) is $15 per visit, so it isn't free.
